a and blocking  the democratic agenda absolutely and so  unless we are going to get down and  fight them in these areas  we're just going to keep losing on a lot  of this stuff and we can go back to some  of the clips i played for you  earlier this week here's the clip of uh  from cpac  uh this was an interview with a couple  people at cpac remember this is the  stuff i pointed out and i said  they are smart to fight at this level  pay attention to their children and what  they say when they come home from school  don't criticize listen if there's things  that go against what they've been  teaching their children  then they need to go to a school board  meeting and they do  and they do is what we're learning need  to read the books that our kids are  being forced to read  so that we can have an honest  conversation with them there's a way to  fight back  and the way to do it is use your words  and use your money  go to your schools don't send your kid  to an indoctrination camp  and they're doing it okay here's another  one this was just a random interview i  mean  as far as we know sometimes these are  plants but as far as we know this was a  random interview at cpac  um uh uh and listen right away to what  this woman i believe from california  says  sure sure what are you yeah i am from  california  and um i'm an activist and uh i believe  in what we're saying here about getting  involved and stuff  but i think we forget to mention that  how we're going to do that we need to  get back into the neighborhoods  we need to do in california right now we  are organizing  uh precincts and voter registration  we're not talking about voter  registration i i think that's  actually that's a great point i'm glad  you came up to us these people  understand it now am i saying the left  doesn't understand it no  i think the left probably does  understand it i think the left probably  does understand it but  they're crushing us on this stuff and so  i am restating  the school boa